      "id": "claim_80d2fb637e374fd1b2373e7269787859",
      "statement": "Migrations are not automatic: db/init is only the new-database baseline and later changes live in db/migrations applied by `make migrate`. Locally `make up` brings Postgres up, runs migrate, then starts the backend, and `make seed` depends on migrate; both are skipped for a managed database (ENV=staging or the bundled Postgres switched off), where migrating is a deliberate separate step.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L65-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:78f0ed37335d7e584e16d38ca2eac0c978ebee5e4cdcd91c721fba827465b47e:"
        }
